Z||000000||87FieroGTx||09-17-2001||12:33 AM|||| Does manualy shifting an Auto trans hurt it? Like downshifting befor a corner?<P> Oh and will it improve performance?||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||09-17-2001||12:41 AM||||I am not sure on the damage issue, I would like to hear the same.  But all I know is, you can drive the auto's like a manual in the way you push the pedal.  I know if I want to accelerate into a corner I can push down hard on the pedal quick and my car will downshift... HARD... and pull like mad.  I do have a high stall TC that spools up FAST.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000002||8Ball||09-17-2001||12:51 AM||||Well i usually drive my wife's car that way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> her trannie is still doing good.<P>But who knows. Doesn't actually seem like it would be too good on it now that I think about it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||09-17-2001||08:01 AM||||I don't think you are hurting anything anymore than just driving it hard to start with.  Just remember that brakes are easier and cheaper to replace than a transmission.<P>Use engine braking when you need to.||||reg||1
